l,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Agent mode will sometimes not use the most recent version of a file and instead seemingly using an old cached version, and edit that. In my case this has led to **destructive** behavior where I simply lost recent updates to code because it was all overwritten by the cached version with some edits here and there.\n\nMy guess is that the most recent version of a file is not correctly uploaded or included when sending it to the API. So the API is re-using some older cache for context.\n\n- Copilot Chat Extension Version: 0.28.0\n- VS Code Version: 1.101.1\n- OS Version: Windows 11 24H2 **but using remote development via SSH**\n- Feature (e.g. agent/edit/ask mode): agent mode\n- Selected model (e.g. GPT 4.1, Claude 3.7 Sonnet): any remote, API-based model\n- Logs: could not find the logs?\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n\n1. work on a repository (git-enabled) over SSH on a linux remote\n2. use agent mode often and `git add .` from time to time\n3. after a while the agent mode will make changes to a file from the cache rather than the last update file, removing recent changes to the file\n","closed_by":{"login":"bhavyaus","id":25044782,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MDQ0Nzgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25044782?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus","html_url":"https://github.com/bhavyaus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavy